  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Tuesday 15 December 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\n4 BEDROOMS | 2.5 BATHROOMS | 689m² FREEHOLD | TORBAY\r\n\r\nYou don’t stay in a home for 24 years without a good reason. Since 2002, one family has called 25 Cottam Grove home. Now, for the first time in more than two decades, it’s someone else’s turn.\r\n\r\nSet on a generous 689m² freehold section in a quiet Torbay cul-de-sac, this much-loved four-bedroom home offers approximately 180m² of floor area, privacy, and the kind of potential that’s harder to find on Auckland’s North Shore.\r\n\r\nLiving and dining areas are welcoming and light-filled. The sunroom is the standout, with an elevated outlook that works just as well for morning coffee as an afternoon read. Four bedrooms and 2.5 bathrooms give flexibility for family life, guests, or a home office, with indoor-outdoor flow for easy summer living.\r\n\r\nA few more reasons to look:\r\n\r\n• 689m² freehold land with space, privacy, and future possibilities\r\n\r\n• Approximately 180m² of practical family living\r\n\r\n• Sunroom with an elevated outlook\r\n\r\n• Double carport, generous storage, and insect screens throughout\r\n\r\n• Solar panels and a DVS ventilation system\r\n\r\n• Well maintained, with room to modernise in your own time\r\n\r\nTorbay is a settled North Shore neighbourhood with shops, supermarkets, cafés, and recreation close by, plus beaches and motorway access a short drive away. The property is zoned for Glamorgan School, Northcross Intermediate, and Long Bay College.\r\n\r\nAfter 24 years of family memories, the next chapter is ready to be written. Contact us to arrange a private viewing.",
